------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED  (production-polished, Apple-idiomatic; no stubs / no skeleton-only / no scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The SwiftUI parity of the web `PlaybackControls` — a CONTROLLED trip-replay transport bar: the host
owns isPlaying / speed / progress / elapsed / total and the bar calls back through onPlay / onPause /
onStop / onSpeedChange / onSeek (+ the keyboard-only onSeekBy / onSpeedRelative / onStepFrame). It
composes a Reset / Play-Pause / Stop trio, a PlaybackSpeedMenu cycling {1,10,25,50,100}×, a
TimelineScrubber (marker ticks + hover/drag preview + drag-to-scrub), a time readout, an optional
keyboard layer (Space/K, ←/→ ∓5s/∓30s, J/L ∓10s, ,/. frame, Home/End, 0–9 percent, +/− speed) with a
transient toast + a help cheatsheet, and a useShortcut registration of that cheatsheet.

The native surface keeps that exact composition as the `content` phase and adds the P4 leaf contract so
it never collapses to a blank box. 14 files (10 app + 1 strings + 3 co-located XCTest):
  PlaybackControls.swift            — bound surface View (binds model; phase switch; .onKeyPress decode)
  PlaybackControls.Model.swift      — Meta(P1/S11), Telemetry seam, i18n facade(P1/S10), Connection,
                                      value types (Speed/Marker/MarkerKind/Preview/Toast), Input, Actions
  PlaybackControls.Seams.swift      — Source protocol + Live + InMemory; ShortcutRegistry seam (P1/S8)
  PlaybackControls.Projection.swift — pure snapshot→resolved (data adapter) + a11y label builders
  PlaybackControls.Keyboard.swift   — key→intent resolver + toast wording + cheatsheet (web keydown)
  PlaybackControls.Store.swift      — @MainActor @Observable state-holder (P1/S8): intents, toast,
                                      once-only view.opened, stale auto-refresh, registry lifecycle
  PlaybackControls.Views.swift      — transport trio, speed control, time readout, help popover, toast,
                                      freshness chip
  PlaybackControls.Scrubber.swift   — native TimelineScrubber (drag/markers/preview, adjustable a11y)
  PlaybackControls.States.swift     — loading skeleton bar, empty (nothing to replay), error+retry
  PlaybackControls.Previews.swift   — #Preview for every state/composition (DEBUG)
  PlaybackControls.strings          — 48 i18n keys (web t() keys + native chrome) — declared==used
  PlaybackControls.Tests.swift / .ModelTests.swift / .KeyboardTests.swift — 57 XCTest

States rendered (all): loading (skeleton bar) · empty (web has none → "Nothing to replay" leaf) ·
error (web QueryError peer + retry) · content (the interactive bar) · stale/offline (freshness chip
with a one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition; last content stays visible).
Precedence: error > loading > empty(durationMs<=0) > content.

Web-source branches reproduced (parity, not shortcuts): the Reset+Stop both → onStop; play/pause toggle;
the speed cycle (tap=nextSpeed, context-menu=any/shiftSpeed); the scrubber drag-to-scrub with throttled
intermediate seeks (SCRUB_INTERVAL_MS=50ms) + final emit; keyframe marker ticks (8 kinds) with
tap-to-seek + tooltip + clustered-count badge; the hover/drag preview (time + speed/power/soc/elevation,
host-formatted); the ariaValueText "m:ss"; the full keydown map incl. Shift escalation (∓5s→∓30s) and
the onSeekBy/onSpeedRelative fallbacks; the transient 900ms shortcut toast; the help cheatsheet (7 rows);
and useShortcut register-on-appear / unregister-on-disappear.

Shared atoms reused (web → native, P1/S9 tokens — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex, no neon body text):
TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel), TSSkeleton, TSEmptyState (web EmptyState), TSQueryError (web QueryError),
TSMaterial.overlay, Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius/TSMotion. The atomic TSPlaybackControls /
TSTimelineScrubber / TSPlaybackSpeedMenu in Sources/Components are the P4 component-library bundle
(OUT OF SCOPE); this surface is the bound, state-aware, telemetry-emitting shell named `PlaybackControls`
— ALL my public types are `PlaybackControls*`-prefixed (verified collision-free; both SDKs compiled the
real Sources/Components+Design alongside this surface with 0 errors).
Telemetry: `view.opened` emitted exactly once with surface slug "PlaybackControls" (P1/S11).
Accessibility: every control labelled (Reset/Play-Pause/Stop/Speed/Help), play-pause label toggles,
the scrubber is an accessibilityAdjustableAction slider with valuetext, markers carry spoken labels,
the toast uses .updatesFrequently, Dynamic-Type fonts, Reduce-Motion honoured (TSSkeleton + playhead).

